2026-08-06T15:21:46.5865945Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5866231Z [36;1m# Do NOT export UserNM here, however tempting the `UserNM=true` trick[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5866691Z [36;1m# from AGENTS.md looks. It is a development shortcut, not a CI setting.[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5867035Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5867256Z [36;1m# R takes the nm program from $UserNM in[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5867632Z [36;1m# tools:::read_symbols_from_object_file, and that function serves two[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5868082Z [36;1m# callers, not one: building `symbols.rds` at install time (which[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5868469Z [36;1m# src/Makevars puts on the `all:` target), *and*[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5868865Z [36;1m# tools:::check_so_symbols scanning the built .so during `R CMD check`.[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5869431Z [36;1m# Pointing nm at `true` blinds the second one, so the check finds no[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5869916Z [36;1m# symbols at all and reports "Found no calls to 'R_registerRoutines',[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5870378Z [36;1m# 'R_useDynamicSymbols'" -- a NOTE, and with error_on = "note" a failed[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5870825Z [36;1m# check on a package that registers its routines perfectly well.[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5871173Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5871472Z [36;1m# It is not worth scoping to the installs either: measured, the sweep is[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5871912Z [36;1m# ~0.25 s per 90 MB of unstripped objects, so ~10-20 s for the whole[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5872478Z [36;1m# ~2.5 GB tree -- under 5% of a commit's floor, against a footgun that[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5872837Z [36;1m# silently weakens a CRAN check.[0m
2026-08-06T15:21:46.5873106Z [36;1m[0m
